{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217698047,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-827c6b39e13df566","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 169"},"output":"title:\tResearch: jq expressiveness lost under a zip or no-default Vec-op-Vec\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t169\n--\nFollow-up research requested in the multiplicity-and-offload-round2 grilling round (question binary-op-default-multiplicity): before choosing between a zip/broadcast default (option B) and no default at all (option C) for binary operators over two same-typed Vecs, survey real jq idioms that rely on the cartesian default and work out concretely what breaks or gets more verbose under B or C. Use real jq snippets with toylang-under-B and toylang-under-C equivalents. Write findings to plans/.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tResearch: jq expressiveness lost under a zip or no-default Vec-op-Vec\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t169\n--\nFollow-up research requested in the multiplicity-and-offload-round2 grilling round (question binary-op-default-multiplicity): before choosing between a zip/broadcast default (option B) and no default at all (option C) for binary operators over two same-typed Vecs, survey real jq idioms that rely on the cartesian default and work out concretely what breaks or gets more verbose under B or C. Use real jq snippets with toylang-under-B and toylang-under-C equivalents. Write findings to plans/.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 169","time":{"start":1788217698032,"end":1788217698042}},"metadata":{"openr