{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217710803,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-978398177443b03b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"cartesian\\|zip\\|broadcast\" draft.md | sed -n '1,5p'; echo \"===\"; sed -n '1310,1320p' draft.md"},"output":"283:One connection: adopting projection semantics pulls [the binary-operator question](plans/questions.md#q2-binary-operators-over-two-multi-valued-expressions-cartesian-zip-or-explicit) (cartesian vs. zip) toward\n284:broadcast, because multidimensional projection and elementwise broadcast are the same tradition.\n285:[That question](plans/questions.md#q2-binary-operators-over-two-multi-valued-expressions-cartesian-zip-or-explicit) and this TODO may be one question.\n1095:Arithmetic on tensors broadcasts, so `$m * 2` is elementwise. That extension is confined to the\n1187:{a:1} | .a =  (1,2)      # -> {a:1}, {a:2}    cartesian\n===\n| | jq | here |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.[]` on an object | iterates values | error; use `to_entries` |\n| `.[]` at top level | many outputs | one value; there is no stream |\n| `.[9]` out of range | `null` | `Opt` |\n| `null \\| .[0]` | `null` | error |\n| `[.[] + .[]]` | cartesian, `[2,3,3,4]` | not expressible by accident |\n\n### Settled\n\n**One bracket per dimension**, left to right: `v[3][]`, not `v[3, ]`. This is already jq's\n","metadata":{"output":"283:One connection: adopting projection semantics pulls [the binary-operator question](plans/questions.md#q2-binary-operators-over-two-multi-valued-expressions-cartesian-zip-or-explicit) (cartesian vs. zip) toward\n284:broadcast, because multidimensional projection and elementwise broadcast are the same tradition.\n285:[That question](plans/questions.md#q2-binary-operators-over-two-multi-valued-expressions-cartesian-zip-or-explicit) and this TODO may be one question.\n1095:Arithmetic on tensors broadcasts, so `$m * 2` is elementwise. That extension is confined to the\n1187:{a:1} | .a =  (1,2)      # -> {a:1}, {a:2}    cartesian\n===\n| | jq | here |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.[]` on an object | iterates values | error; use `to_entries` |\n| `.[]` at top level | many outputs | one value; there is no stream |\n| `.[9]` out of range | `null` | `Opt` |\n| `null \\| .[0]` | `null` | error |\n| `[.[] + .[]]` | cartesian, `[2,3,3,4]` | not expressible by accident |\n\n### Settled\n\n**One bracket per dimension**, left to right: `v[3][]`, not `v[3, ]`. This is already jq's\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"cartesian\\|zip\\|broadcast\" draft.md | sed -n '1,5p'; echo \"===\"; sed -n '1310,1320p' draft.md","time":{"start":1788217710794,"end":1788217710797}},"id":"prt_05a14d659001Ouy2eKHSJxBtPi","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","messageID":"msg_05a14d1b30014uUVG2zhLcsWOq"}}
