{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217726384,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9acca5297e680a64","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls examples/ | head -30; echo \"===\"; cat prelude.toy | head -60"},"output":"adults.toy\nfilter.toy\nfizzbuzz.toy\ngreet_fn.toy\ngreet.toy\nhello.toy\nshapes.toy\n===\npub enum Opt<T> { some(T), none }\n\npub enum Result<T, E> { ok(T), err(E) }\n\npub fn join_lines(v: Vec<Str>) -> Str =\n    \"\" if length(v) == 0 else\n        v[0]! if length(v) == 1 else\n        v[0]! + \"\\n\" + join_lines(tail(v)!)\n\npub fn join(v: Vec<Str>) -> Str =\n    \"\" if length(v) == 0 else v[0]! + join(tail(v)!)\n","metadata":{"output":"adults.toy\nfilter.toy\nfizzbuzz.toy\ngreet_fn.toy\ngreet.toy\nhello.toy\nshapes.toy\n===\npub enum Opt<T> { some(T), none }\n\npub enum Result<T, E> { ok(T), err(E) }\n\npub fn join_lines(v: Vec<Str>) -> Str =\n    \"\" if length(v) == 0 else\n        v[0]! if length(v) == 1 else\n        v[0]! + \"\\n\" + join_lines(tail(v)!)\n\npub fn join(v: Vec<Str>) -> Str =\n    \"\" if length(v) == 0 else v[0]! + join(tail(v)!)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls examples/ | head -30; echo \"===\"; cat prelude.toy | head -60","time":{"start":1788217726382,"end":1788217726383}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I now have a good understanding. toylang has no streams; there is `Vec`, and operators over Vec operands are the open question Q2. There's also the projection/multidimensional angle. toylang uses `[]` as projection.\n\nLet me understand the syntax better — how does toylang write things? Let me look at examples and the prelude to understand concrete toylang syntax (function calls, named builtins like `zip`, `cross`). Let me look at a couple of example files and the operator section.\n\nLet me also check how operators are currently spelled in toylang (e.g. `+`, `-`, `==`). And how named builtins are called, e.g. `flatten`. Let me check the prelude.toy and some example files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a1514cb001iIzU5KoszYwKx7","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","messageID":"msg_05a150827001KvjWrgDM9PZuyt"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1788217726391,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","part":{"id":"prt_05a1515b5001AnymCsIergK9D1","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"6a598f8a24b34371f9755203ce4bf243b87859cd","messageID":"msg_05a150827001KvjWrgDM9PZuyt","sessionID":"ses_fa5eb6461ffeMsD7uLAy4rsiUF","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":27619,"input":1019,"output":61,"reasoning":171,"cache":{"write":0,"read":26368}},"cost":0.000529883}}
